Maps:
1.  Hashmaps are used to store key value pairs.
2.  We can create HashMap, HashTable and LinkedHashMap in java.
3.  We can also create TreeMap that is a kind of SortedMap.
4.  A Map cannot contain duplicate keys.
5.  Each key can map to at most 1 value.
6.  HashTable is synchronized and slow while HashMap is not synchronized.
7.  Hashtable does not allow null key/values.
8.  HashMap allows one null key and any number of null values.
9.  LinkedHashMaps maintain insertion order.
10. TreeMap adds data in natural sorted order.